  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "One or two given names and a family name from the father, though couples may choose either name. Austrian family names come from farms, trades and places (Gruber, Huber, Bauer, Pichler); Vienna is full of Czech surnames from the old empire (Novotny, Swoboda, Prohaska). Academic titles are part of how people are addressed: Frau Magistra, Herr Diplomingenieur, Herr Doktor. Families from Bosnia, Croatia, Serbia, Turkey, Poland and Romania keep their own names.",
